Only the CSVs pass the test: $4{,}000{,}000 + 2{,}500{,}000 = \mathbf{6{,}500{,}000}$ bytes (readme.md excluded).

(b) 180 us $= 180{,}000$ ns. With 3 entries iterated, the cost is $180{,}000 / 3 = \mathbf{60{,}000}$ ns (60 us) per entry, the readme.md entry is visited but contributes nothing to the sum.

(c)

```cpp
// C++20
auto csvSizes = fs::directory_iterator("data/ticks")
              | std::views::filter([](const auto& e) {
                    return e.is_regular_file() && e.path().extension() == ".csv"; })
              | std::views::transform([](const auto& e) { return e.file_size(); });
```

`std::views::filter`, `std::views::transform` and the `|` pipe are C++20-only; the directory iterator becomes a proper range in C++20. Summing over this lazy pipeline yields the same 6,500,000 bytes without building any intermediate container.

